 * Production  (NODE_ENV !== 'development'):
 *   Every call to getSecret(name) fetches the secret value from AWS Secrets
 *   Manager.  The secret is expected to be stored as a JSON object whose
 *   top-level keys match the names listed in .env.test (e.g. DATABASE_URL,
 *   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY …).  A per-process in-memory cache avoids redundant
 *   network round-trips within a single Lambda invocation / server process.
